{% comment %}
  Renders the storefront Warranty Claim Form (Slice 5 task 5-5,
  docs/WARRANTY-CLAIMS.md, docs/specs/SLICE-5-WARRANTY-CLAIMS.md criteria
  153-156). POSTs to `POST /apps/carat/warranty-claim`
  (app/app/routes/apps.carat.warranty-claim.tsx) via
  `assets/warranty-claim-form.js` -- a plain `<form>`, NOT Shopify's native
  `{% form %}` tag, because there is no native Shopify form type for a
  custom App Proxy submission (same reasoning as
  `snippets/bank-payment-checkout-dialog.liquid`, whose field/error markup
  conventions this file follows closely: `.field`/`.field__input`/
  `.field__label`/`.field--with-error` and `.form-status`/`.form__message`
  are all EXISTING Dawn classes reused here, not reinvented).

  COPY STATUS -- read before editing any string in this file or its locale
  keys. THREE strings are owner-approved and evidence-pinned, not draft:
  the acknowledgment text and its affirmative-action label
  (`templates.warranty_claim.form.acknowledgment_text` /
  `.acknowledgment_affirm_label`, imported byte-for-byte from
  `app/app/domain/warranty/acknowledgmentText.ts`'s
  `WARRANTY_CLAIM_ACKNOWLEDGMENT_TEXT` /
  `_AFFIRMATIVE_ACTION_LABEL`, proven identical by
  `app/app/domain/warranty/acknowledgmentThemeLocale.test.ts`), and the
  account-required gate sentence, `.sign_in_required_message`, which carries
  the exact owner-approved sentence from
  `docs/REQUIRED-CUSTOMER-ACCOUNTS.md` §4 ("Please sign in or create a
  CaratForUs account to continue.") -- pinned in
  `app/app/theme/ownerApprovedCopy.test.ts` alongside the identical sentence
  in `snippets/bank-payment-checkout-dialog.liquid`. EVERY OTHER string in
  this file's locale keys -- the intro, the notice, every field label
  (including the new order-lookup/picker copy), every error and the
  confirmation copy -- is DRAFT, not yet through an owner-approval pass
  (spec §11 owner item 2 names exactly this form's copy as needing approval
  before shipping is complete; see this task's handoff for the full
  explanation). Drafted as closely as possible from ALREADY-LOCKED language
  in `docs/WARRANTY-CLAIMS.md` §1/§3/§9 rather than invented from scratch,
  and shipped functional per the architect's instruction rather than
  blocked on that approval -- matching the SAME precedent already in this
  theme: `snippets/bank-payment-checkout-dialog.liquid`'s own header
  comment marks its `bank_payment_checkout_form.*` keys "DRAFT pending
  owner approval" too.

  CRITERION 156 -- THE ONE THIS FILE IS MOST CAREFUL ABOUT. No address, no
  "send it to us", no shipping instruction anywhere in this file, its locale
  keys, or its JS -- not in the intro, not in the notice, not in the
  confirmation. `WARRANTY-CLAIMS.md` §3 requires CaratForUs to authorize
  inspection first, and criterion 156 is explicit that the system NEVER
  issues shipping instructions before that authorization -- not in this
  form, not in a status page, not in an email, and this form is none of
  those places. The confirmation view (post-submit) states plainly that
  the customer will be contacted before authorization, not to send the
  item, and gives no address, no timeframe, and no local-jeweller mention
  (criterion 165 -- see below).

  NO LOCAL JEWELLER, ANYWHERE (criterion 165). Not drafted, not mentioned,
  not a form option. That path is internal-only until CaratForUs authorizes
  it for one specific resolved claim (`WARRANTY-CLAIMS.md` §7).

  NO TURNAROUND TIME, NO REMEDY IMPLICATION (§12/P1/P2). No "shortly", no
  "as soon as possible", no promise of repair over replacement/refund
  anywhere in this file's copy.

  UPLOADS -- OMITTED, NOT FAKED. `docs/specs/SLICE-5-WARRANTY-CLAIMS.md` §5:
  the R2 bucket does not exist and all four `STORAGE_*` env vars are empty
  in every environment. Building a file-input control here would either do
  nothing when clicked or silently drop whatever the customer selected --
  both worse than not offering it. This form has NO upload control at all;
  `templates.warranty_claim.form.uploads_note` tells the customer plainly
  (with no internal-infrastructure reason attached -- "isn't available in
  this form yet", never "our storage bucket isn't provisioned") that photos/
  video aren't collected here yet, and invites them to mention that fact in
  the problem description instead. `shopifyVariantId` is similarly not
  collected as an explicit visible field -- see the JS file's own comment on
  why it is a best-effort, query-string-only convenience rather than
  something asked of the customer directly.

  ORDER ID / LINE ITEM ID -- NOW RESOLVED VIA AN ORDER PICKER, NOT A RAW
  GID FIELD. The intake route's contract (`apps.carat.warranty-claim.tsx`)
  still resolves `orderRef`/`lineRef` against Shopify's numeric Order/
  LineItem GIDs, and that contract is unchanged. What changed is where
  those GIDs come from: the customer now types the order number they
  actually know (e.g. "1001") into a picker driven by
  `POST /apps/carat/warranty-order-lookup`
  (`apps.carat.warranty-order-lookup.tsx`, an AUTHENTICATED-ONLY route --
  see its own module comment) and chooses a line item from the resulting
  list; `assets/warranty-claim-form.js` fills the still-present
  `#WarrantyClaimOrderId`/`#WarrantyClaimLineItemId` inputs (now `hidden`,
  not visible text fields) from that response. The customer never sees or
  types a GID. `?order_id=`/`?line_item_id=`/`?variant_id=` query-string
  pre-fill (`prefillFromQueryString` in the JS file) is UNCHANGED and still
  targets those same hidden inputs by `name` -- it still has no real caller
  today, and remains a possible future deep-link seam (e.g. from an order-
  confirmation email), not something this task builds.

  THE LOOKUP ROUTE COLLAPSES "DOESN'T EXIST" AND "ISN'T YOURS" INTO ONE
  GENERIC OUTCOME (its own module comment explains why -- anti-enumeration
  by construction). This form and its JS never try to infer or display the
  distinction even though the route's `{ resolved: false }` is
  indistinguishable either way; `templates.warranty_claim.form
  .order_lookup_not_found` is worded generically for exactly that reason,
  and directs an unresolved search to Customer Care
  (`docs/REQUIRED-CUSTOMER-ACCOUNTS.md` §5) rather than inventing a guest
  fallback.

  CLIENT-SIDE GATING IS UX, NOT ENFORCEMENT. Both the sign-in gate below
  and the order picker only avoid walking a signed-out or GID-less customer
  into a submission that cannot succeed. The actual authorization is the
  401 in `apps.carat.warranty-order-lookup.tsx`/`apps.carat.warranty-
  claim.tsx`, exactly the same division of labour as `snippets/bank-
  payment-checkout-dialog.liquid`'s own header comment describes for Bank
  Payment Checkout.

  ACCOUNT REQUIRED (`docs/REQUIRED-CUSTOMER-ACCOUNTS.md` §5, a locked owner
  decision). A signed-out shopper (`customer` is `nil`) never sees the
  order picker or the rest of the form -- only a sign-in requirement (see
  the `customer` conditional around the `<form>` below), matching the
  pattern already proven in `snippets/bank-payment-checkout-dialog.liquid`.
  This is a server-side render-time branch on Liquid's own `customer`
  object, not a client-side hide-after-render.

  Accepts (schema settings): heading (optional override).
{% endcomment %}
{{ 'component-warranty-claim-form.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- style -%}
  .section-{{ section.id }}-padding {
    padding-top: {{ section.settings.padding_top | times: 0.75 | round: 0 }}px;
    padding-bottom: {{ section.settings.padding_bottom | times: 0.75 | round: 0 }}px;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .section-{{ section.id }}-padding {
      padding-top: {{ section.settings.padding_top }}px;
      padding-bottom: {{ section.settings.padding_bottom }}px;
    }
  }
{%- endstyle -%}

<div class="color-{{ section.settings.color_scheme }} gradient">
  <div class="page-width page-width--narrow section-{{ section.id }}-padding carat-warranty-claim">
    {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
      <h2 class="title title-wrapper--no-top-margin {{ section.settings.heading_size }}">
        {{ section.settings.heading }}
      </h2>
    {%- else -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Visually hidden when unset, matching contact-form.liquid's own
        treatment -- `sections/main-page.liquid` (rendered first in
        templates/page.warranty-claim.json) already shows the Shopify page's
        own title as an <h1>; a second VISIBLE heading here would duplicate
        it for a merchant who titled that page "Warranty Claim".
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <h2 class="visually-hidden">{{ 'templates.warranty_claim.form.heading' | t }}</h2>
    {%- endif -%}

    <p class="carat-warranty-claim__intro">
      {{- 'templates.warranty_claim.form.intro' | t -}}
    </p>

    {%- comment -%}
      Criterion 156 -- always visible, ahead of every field, never behind a
      toggle. Not a warning about a fault; a plain statement of process.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="carat-warranty-claim__notice" role="note">
      <p class="carat-warranty-claim__notice-heading">
        {{- 'templates.warranty_claim.form.notice_heading' | t -}}
      </p>
      <p class="carat-warranty-claim__notice-body">
        {{- 'templates.warranty_claim.form.notice_body' | t -}}
      </p>
    </div>

    <div
      id="WarrantyClaimErrorSummary"
      class="carat-warranty-claim__error-summary form-status-list"
      role="alert"
      tabindex="-1"
      hidden
      data-carat-warranty-error-summary
    ></div>

    <div
      id="WarrantyClaimConfirmation"
      class="carat-warranty-claim__confirmation"
      role="status"
      tabindex="-1"
      hidden
      data-carat-warranty-confirmation
    ></div>

    {%- if customer -%}
    <form id="WarrantyClaimForm" novalidate data-carat-warranty-form>
      <fieldset class="carat-warranty-claim__fieldset" data-carat-warranty-order-picker>
        <legend class="carat-warranty-claim__legend">
          {{- 'templates.warranty_claim.form.order_lookup_legend' | t }}
          <span aria-hidden="true">*</span>
        </legend>

        <div class="carat-warranty-claim__field-row" data-carat-warranty-order-search>
          <div class="field field--with-error">
            <input
              type="text"
              id="WarrantyClaimOrderNumber"
              class="field__input"
              inputmode="numeric"
              autocomplete="off"
              placeholder="{{ 'templates.warranty_claim.form.order_number_placeholder' | t }}"
              aria-describedby="WarrantyClaimOrderNumber-help WarrantyClaimOrderNumber-error"
              data-carat-warranty-order-number-input
            >
            <label class="field__label" for="WarrantyClaimOrderNumber">
              {{- 'templates.warranty_claim.form.order_number_label' | t -}}
            </label>
            <small id="WarrantyClaimOrderNumber-help" class="carat-warranty-claim__field-help">
              {{- 'templates.warranty_claim.form.order_number_help' | t -}}
            </small>
            <small
              id="WarrantyClaimOrderNumber-error"
              class="carat-warranty-claim__field-error form__message"
              hidden
              data-carat-warranty-field-error
            >
              <span class="svg-wrapper">{{- 'icon-error.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}</span>
              <span data-carat-warranty-field-error-text></span>
            </small>
          </div>
          <button type="button" class="button button--secondary" data-carat-warranty-lookup-submit>
            {{- 'templates.warranty_claim.form.find_order_button' | t -}}
          </button>
        </div>

        <p
          id="WarrantyClaimOrderLookupStatus"
          class="carat-warranty-claim__status form-status"
          role="status"
          aria-live="polite"
          hidden
          data-carat-warranty-order-lookup-status
        ></p>

        {%- comment -%}
          Populated by JS only after a successful lookup -- see the JS
          file's `wireOrderLookup`. `tabindex="-1"` + a `.focus()` call on
          reveal moves focus here so a screen reader user is told a result
          appeared, matching the pattern this theme already uses for the
          error summary and confirmation regions above.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="carat-warranty-claim__order-result" hidden tabindex="-1" data-carat-warranty-order-result>
          <p class="carat-warranty-claim__order-result-summary" data-carat-warranty-order-result-summary></p>

          <fieldset class="carat-warranty-claim__fieldset carat-warranty-claim__fieldset--nested">
            <legend class="carat-warranty-claim__legend">
              {{- 'templates.warranty_claim.form.select_item_legend' | t }}
              <span aria-hidden="true">*</span>
            </legend>
            <div
              class="carat-warranty-claim__radio-group carat-warranty-claim__radio-group--stacked"
              data-carat-warranty-line-item-options
            ></div>
            <small
              id="WarrantyClaimLineItemPicker-error"
              class="carat-warranty-claim__field-error form__message"
              hidden
              data-carat-warranty-field-error
            >
              <span class="svg-wrapper">{{- 'icon-error.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}</span>
              <span data-carat-warranty-field-error-text></span>
            </small>
          </fieldset>

          <button type="button" class="link" data-carat-warranty-order-search-again>
            {{- 'templates.warranty_claim.form.search_different_order' | t -}}
          </button>
        </div>

        <p class="carat-warranty-claim__field-help">
          {{- 'templates.warranty_claim.form.cant_find_order_help' | t -}}
        </p>
      </fieldset>

      {%- comment -%}
        Filled by JS from the resolved order-lookup response, never typed by
        the customer directly -- see this section's own header comment
        ("ORDER ID / LINE ITEM ID") and `warranty-claim-form.js`'s
        `wireOrderLookup`. No `required` attribute: hidden inputs are not
        subject to native constraint validation, and `validate()` below
        already enforces both are non-empty before submission.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <input type="hidden" id="WarrantyClaimOrderId" name="order_id" value="">
      <input type="hidden" id="WarrantyClaimLineItemId" name="line_item_id" value="">

      {%- comment -%}
        Best-effort convenience only, never asked of the customer directly --
        see this section's own header comment and the JS file's comment on
        `variant_id`. Populated from `?variant_id=` when present; otherwise
        left blank and simply omitted from the submitted request.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <input type="hidden" id="WarrantyClaimVariantId" name="variant_id" value="">

      <div class="field field--with-error">
        <input
          type="text"
          id="WarrantyClaimPurchaserName"
          name="purchaser_name"
          class="field__input"
          autocomplete="name"
          required
          value="{{ customer.name | escape }}"
          aria-describedby="WarrantyClaimPurchaserName-error"
        >
        <label class="field__label" for="WarrantyClaimPurchaserName">
          {{- 'templates.warranty_claim.form.purchaser_name_label' | t }}
          <span aria-hidden="true">*</span></label
        >
        <small
          id="WarrantyClaimPurchaserName-error"
          class="carat-warranty-claim__field-error form__message"
          hidden
          data-carat-warranty-field-error
        >
          <span class="svg-wrapper">{{- 'icon-error.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}</span>
          <span data-carat-warranty-field-error-text></span>
        </small>
      </div>

      <div class="field field--with-error">
        <input
          type="email"
          id="WarrantyClaimPurchaserEmail"
          name="purchaser_email"
          class="field__input"
          autocomplete="email"
          spellcheck="false"
          autocapitalize="off"
          required
          value="{{ customer.email | escape }}"
          aria-describedby="WarrantyClaimPurchaserEmail-error"
        >
        <label class="field__label" for="WarrantyClaimPurchaserEmail">
          {{- 'templates.warranty_claim.form.purchaser_email_label' | t }}
          <span aria-hidden="true">*</span></label
        >
        <small
          id="WarrantyClaimPurchaserEmail-error"
          class="carat-warranty-claim__field-error form__message"
          hidden
          data-carat-warranty-field-error
        >
          <span class="svg-wrapper">{{- 'icon-error.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}</span>
          <span data-carat-warranty-field-error-text></span>
        </small>
      </div>

      <div class="field field--with-error">
        <textarea
          id="WarrantyClaimItemConfiguration"
          name="item_configuration"
          class="text-area field__input"
          rows="3"
          required
          placeholder="{{ 'templates.warranty_claim.form.item_configuration_placeholder' | t }}"
          aria-describedby="WarrantyClaimItemConfiguration-error"
        ></textarea>
        <label class="form__label field__label" for="WarrantyClaimItemConfiguration">
          {{- 'templates.warranty_claim.form.item_configuration_label' | t }}
          <span aria-hidden="true">*</span></label
        >
        <small
          id="WarrantyClaimItemConfiguration-error"
          class="carat-warranty-claim__field-error form__message"
          hidden
          data-carat-warranty-field-error
        >
          <span class="svg-wrapper">{{- 'icon-error.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}</span>
          <span data-carat-warranty-field-error-text></span>
        </small>
      </div>

      <div class="carat-warranty-claim__field-row carat-warranty-claim__field-row--three">
        <div class="field">
          <label class="field__label field__label--static" for="WarrantyClaimPurchaseDate">
            {{- 'templates.warranty_claim.form.purchase_date_label' | t -}}
          </label>
          <input type="date" id="WarrantyClaimPurchaseDate" name="purchase_date" class="field__input">
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label class="field__label field__label--static" for="WarrantyClaimDeliveryDate">
            {{- 'templates.warranty_claim.form.delivery_date_label' | t -}}
          </label>
          <input type="date" id="WarrantyClaimDeliveryDate" name="delivery_date" class="field__input">
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label class="field__label field__label--static" for="WarrantyClaimIssueNoticedDate">
            {{- 'templates.warranty_claim.form.issue_first_noticed_date_label' | t -}}
          </label>
          <input type="date" id="WarrantyClaimIssueNoticedDate" name="issue_first_noticed_date" class="field__input">
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="field field--with-error">
        <textarea
          id="WarrantyClaimProblemDescription"
          name="problem_description"
          class="text-area field__input"
          rows="6"
          required
          aria-describedby="WarrantyClaimProblemDescription-error"
        ></textarea>
        <label class="form__label field__label" for="WarrantyClaimProblemDescription">
          {{- 'templates.warranty_claim.form.problem_description_label' | t }}
          <span aria-hidden="true">*</span></label
        >
        <small
          id="WarrantyClaimProblemDescription-error"
          class="carat-warranty-claim__field-error form__message"
          hidden
          data-carat-warranty-field-error
        >
          <span class="svg-wrapper">{{- 'icon-error.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}</span>
          <span data-carat-warranty-field-error-text></span>
        </small>
      </div>

      <p class="carat-warranty-claim__uploads-note">
        {{- 'templates.warranty_claim.form.uploads_note' | t -}}
      </p>

      <fieldset class="carat-warranty-claim__fieldset">
        <legend class="carat-warranty-claim__legend">
          {{- 'templates.warranty_claim.form.impact_question_label' | t }}
          <span aria-hidden="true">*</span>
        </legend>
        <div class="carat-warranty-claim__radio-group">
          <label class="carat-warranty-claim__radio">
            <input type="radio" name="had_impact_or_damage_event" value="yes" required data-carat-warranty-impact-radio>
            {{- 'templates.warranty_claim.form.impact_yes' | t -}}
          </label>
          <label class="carat-warranty-claim__radio">
            <input type="radio" name="had_impact_or_damage_event" value="no" required data-carat-warranty-impact-radio>
            {{- 'templates.warranty_claim.form.impact_no' | t -}}
          </label>
        </div>
        <div class="field field--with-error" id="WarrantyClaimImpactDetailsWrapper" hidden data-carat-warranty-impact-details-wrapper>
          <textarea
            id="WarrantyClaimImpactDetails"
            name="impact_or_damage_details"
            class="text-area field__input"
            rows="3"
            aria-describedby="WarrantyClaimImpactDetails-error"
          ></textarea>
          <label class="form__label field__label" for="WarrantyClaimImpactDetails">
            {{- 'templates.warranty_claim.form.impact_details_label' | t -}}
          </label>
          <small
            id="WarrantyClaimImpactDetails-error"
            class="carat-warranty-claim__field-error form__message"
            hidden
            data-carat-warranty-field-error
          >
            <span class="svg-wrapper">{{- 'icon-error.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}</span>
            <span data-carat-warranty-field-error-text></span>
          </small>
        </div>
      </fieldset>

      <fieldset class="carat-warranty-claim__fieldset">
        <legend class="carat-warranty-claim__legend">
          {{- 'templates.warranty_claim.form.altered_question_label' | t }}
          <span aria-hidden="true">*</span>
        </legend>
        <div class="carat-warranty-claim__radio-group">
          <label class="carat-warranty-claim__radio">
            <input type="radio" name="was_altered_after_delivery" value="yes" required data-carat-warranty-altered-radio>
            {{- 'templates.warranty_claim.form.altered_yes' | t -}}
          </label>
          <label class="carat-warranty-claim__radio">
            <input type="radio" name="was_altered_after_delivery" value="no" required data-carat-warranty-altered-radio>
            {{- 'templates.warranty_claim.form.altered_no' | t -}}
          </label>
        </div>
        <div class="field field--with-error" id="WarrantyClaimAlterationDetailsWrapper" hidden data-carat-warranty-alteration-details-wrapper>
          <textarea
            id="WarrantyClaimAlterationDetails"
            name="alteration_details"
            class="text-area field__input"
            rows="3"
            aria-describedby="WarrantyClaimAlterationDetails-error"
          ></textarea>
          <label class="form__label field__label" for="WarrantyClaimAlterationDetails">
            {{- 'templates.warranty_claim.form.altered_details_label' | t -}}
          </label>
          <small
            id="WarrantyClaimAlterationDetails-error"
            class="carat-warranty-claim__field-error form__message"
            hidden
            data-carat-warranty-field-error
          >
            <span class="svg-wrapper">{{- 'icon-error.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}</span>
            <span data-carat-warranty-field-error-text></span>
          </small>
        </div>
      </fieldset>

      <div class="field">
        <input
          type="text"
          id="WarrantyClaimCertificate"
          name="certificate_or_serial"
          class="field__input"
          placeholder="{{ 'templates.warranty_claim.form.certificate_label' | t }}"
        >
        <label class="field__label" for="WarrantyClaimCertificate">
          {{- 'templates.warranty_claim.form.certificate_label' | t -}}
        </label>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        The ONE owner-approved, evidence-pinned string this form renders --
        see this file's header comment. Never pre-checked (criterion 154 /
        WARRANTY-CLAIMS.md §2's "acknowledgment... does not itself establish
        warranty coverage").
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="carat-warranty-claim__acknowledgment">
        <p id="WarrantyClaimAcknowledgmentText" class="carat-warranty-claim__acknowledgment-text">
          {{- 'templates.warranty_claim.form.acknowledgment_text' | t -}}
        </p>
        <div class="carat-warranty-claim__control">
          <input
            type="checkbox"
            id="WarrantyClaimAcknowledgment"
            name="acknowledgment"
            class="carat-warranty-claim__checkbox"
            required
            aria-describedby="WarrantyClaimAcknowledgmentText WarrantyClaimAcknowledgment-error"
            data-carat-warranty-acknowledgment
          >
          <label for="WarrantyClaimAcknowledgment" class="carat-warranty-claim__checkbox-label">
            {{- 'templates.warranty_claim.form.acknowledgment_affirm_label' | t -}}
          </label>
        </div>
        <small
          id="WarrantyClaimAcknowledgment-error"
          class="carat-warranty-claim__field-error form__message"
          hidden
          data-carat-warranty-field-error
        >
          <span class="svg-wrapper">{{- 'icon-error.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}</span>
          <span data-carat-warranty-field-error-text></span>
        </small>
      </div>

      <div class="carat-warranty-claim__actions">
        <button type="submit" class="button" data-carat-warranty-submit>
          {{- 'templates.warranty_claim.form.submit' | t -}}
        </button>
      </div>

      <p
        id="WarrantyClaimStatus"
        class="carat-warranty-claim__status form-status"
        role="status"
        aria-live="polite"
        hidden
        data-carat-warranty-status
      ></p>
    </form>
    {%- else -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      ACCOUNT REQUIRED (`docs/REQUIRED-CUSTOMER-ACCOUNTS.md` §5) -- see this
      section's own header comment. Real `<h3>` (nested under the section's
      own `<h1>`/`<h2>`/visually-hidden heading above), a plain-text
      owner-approved sentence, and a genuine keyboard-operable sign-in link
      that returns the shopper to this exact page -- same pattern as
      `snippets/bank-payment-checkout-dialog.liquid`'s own signed-out
      branch.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="carat-warranty-claim__signin-required" data-carat-warranty-signin-required>
      <h3 class="carat-warranty-claim__signin-heading">
        {{- 'templates.warranty_claim.form.sign_in_required_heading' | t -}}
      </h3>
      <p class="carat-warranty-claim__signin-message">
        {{- 'templates.warranty_claim.form.sign_in_required_message' | t -}}
      </p>
      <div class="carat-warranty-claim__actions">
        <a
          href="{{ routes.account_login_url }}?return_url={{ request.path | url_encode }}"
          class="button"
          data-carat-warranty-signin-link
        >
          {{- 'customer.log_in' | t -}}
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>

<script src="{{ 'warranty-claim-form.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>

